WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:09.210
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon. Happy
that I am here with you.

00:00:09.211 --> 00:00:13.135
I am coming from Don Bosco,

00:00:13.136 --> 00:00:16.860
you must be knowing about
Don Bosco schools colleges.

00:00:16.861 --> 00:00:19.180
We also work for children on

00:00:19.181 --> 00:00:21.630
the street, abandoned,
missing children.

00:00:21.631 --> 00:00:23.120
There is another unit called

00:00:23.121 --> 00:00:25.410
Don Bosco Young at Risk Forum.

00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:29.310
So, I come from Don Bosco Young
at Risk Forum from Delhi.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.050
Don Bosco YaR Forum,

00:00:33.051 --> 00:00:36.850
it has 174 centers across

00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:40.160
India working for various types

00:00:40.161 --> 00:00:42.240
of children in
collaboration with NGOs,

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:46.560
governments, individuals,
more than 110 years in India.

00:00:46.561 --> 00:00:49.625
We are working in about 20 states

00:00:49.626 --> 00:00:51.455
or the union territories,

00:00:51.456 --> 00:00:55.250
caring for about two lakhs
plus children who

00:00:55.251 --> 00:00:56.900
are in need of care and

00:00:56.901 --> 00:00:59.460
protection and in
conflict with the law.

00:00:59.461 --> 00:01:02.995
Our services are
being on the street,

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.780
meeting the children
were abandoned, missing,

00:01:05.781 --> 00:01:09.460
and giving them shelter,
education, health,

00:01:09.461 --> 00:01:11.970
counseling, vocational training,

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.710
job placement, home placement.

00:01:13.711 --> 00:01:17.395
Finally, settling them
back in the society.

00:01:17.396 --> 00:01:19.580
We also do advocacy with

00:01:19.581 --> 00:01:22.135
the government, creating systems,

00:01:22.136 --> 00:01:24.085
especially for caring
of these kind of

00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:27.460
children or young
people who are at risk,

00:01:27.461 --> 00:01:30.235
including various types
of categories.

00:01:30.236 --> 00:01:34.075
Young at Risk in short,

00:01:34.076 --> 00:01:35.890
safety and growth and

00:01:35.891 --> 00:01:38.460
development and are in need
of care and protection.

00:01:38.461 --> 00:01:42.315
That is what we define
as Young at Risk.

00:01:42.316 --> 00:01:46.700
There are various categories,
including HIV infected,

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:49.460
third-gender, of late
we have been thinking

00:01:49.461 --> 00:01:52.580
about them trying to
start some work for them,

00:01:52.581 --> 00:01:55.055
and school dropouts,
drug addicts,

00:01:55.056 --> 00:01:57.530
those who are sexually

00:01:57.531 --> 00:02:00.315
abused, physically
abused, emotionally,

00:02:00.316 --> 00:02:04.160
and migrants is
another category we have been

00:02:04.161 --> 00:02:08.260
looking at in the past
two, three years,

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.745
and any other category of

00:02:10.746 --> 00:02:14.149
young children at risk
or young people at risk,

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.310
we do include as and when they

00:02:16.311 --> 00:02:19.855
see and in the region
where we work.

00:02:19.856 --> 00:02:23.910
Mission is inspired by
our founder Don Bosco.

00:02:23.911 --> 00:02:25.860
A world where every child,

00:02:25.861 --> 00:02:27.940
every young person
lives and grows towards

00:02:27.941 --> 00:02:31.100
fullness of life,
that's our mission.

00:02:31.101 --> 00:02:32.800
Okay, what do we do,

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.380
different projects that we
do that might interest you

00:02:35.381 --> 00:02:37.060
because when I come here I

00:02:37.061 --> 00:02:39.355
talk to you as technical person.

00:02:39.356 --> 00:02:42.960
When I go down the line
to the NGOs I'm a techie,

00:02:42.961 --> 00:02:45.670
when I go down the line
I had to talk completely

00:02:45.671 --> 00:02:48.640
a different language otherwise
just they throw me out.

00:02:48.641 --> 00:02:52.560
They say you are talking
something above our head.

00:02:52.561 --> 00:02:55.300
The money that you are
asking us to invest on

00:02:55.301 --> 00:02:58.585
technology if we could
save 100 more children,

00:02:58.586 --> 00:03:02.125
that's the kind of
thinking NGOs had, not anymore.

00:03:02.126 --> 00:03:03.820
They are also looking for,

00:03:03.821 --> 00:03:05.890
because every work
is a model that

00:03:05.891 --> 00:03:08.360
we create and it cannot be,

00:03:08.361 --> 00:03:10.160
all the problem in
India we cannot

00:03:10.161 --> 00:03:12.860
solve and we are coming
to a realization,

00:03:12.861 --> 00:03:14.975
especially people who are working

00:03:14.976 --> 00:03:17.660
in NGOs down the line are

00:03:17.661 --> 00:03:20.240
realizing that we
need partnerships and

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:23.060
networks in order to
solve bigger problems,

00:03:23.061 --> 00:03:27.100
all that we do is only a drop
in the ocean under model.

00:03:27.101 --> 00:03:30.545
That's a great realization
that's coming up these days.

00:03:30.546 --> 00:03:34.960
So, we are working in to
develop a biometric app.

00:03:34.961 --> 00:03:37.900
It's already developed
called child BPA.

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:40.460
By which even other is
saying that it is not

00:03:40.461 --> 00:03:43.050
able to track
children's biometric.

00:03:43.051 --> 00:03:44.720
It has got its own problems.

00:03:44.721 --> 00:03:47.350
So, we are trying to
work with Fujitsu,

00:03:47.351 --> 00:03:50.800
trying to get the PAM biometric

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.490
and then we are experimenting in

00:03:52.491 --> 00:03:54.245
Bangalore as well as in Delhi.

00:03:54.246 --> 00:03:55.550
If everything goes well,

00:03:55.551 --> 00:03:57.440
we will integrate it
with our system which

00:03:57.441 --> 00:04:00.560
is already existing
called Child MISS,

00:04:00.561 --> 00:04:03.210
management information
systems and services.

00:04:03.211 --> 00:04:06.395
Migrant is something we
started three years ago,

00:04:06.396 --> 00:04:08.240
Looking at different points

00:04:08.241 --> 00:04:10.095
where we could work
with migrants.

00:04:10.096 --> 00:04:15.200
App is in plan but nothing
has really taken off,

00:04:15.201 --> 00:04:17.425
still the groundwork is going on.

00:04:17.426 --> 00:04:20.180
JJ Alliance is
another important work

00:04:20.181 --> 00:04:21.840
we do in the national level,

00:04:21.841 --> 00:04:23.585
trying to improve the system of

00:04:23.586 --> 00:04:27.920
juvenile justice in
partnership with

00:04:27.921 --> 00:04:30.860
the government and also
educating down the line

00:04:30.861 --> 00:04:32.780
implementing the law as well

00:04:32.781 --> 00:04:34.940
as taking forward the system,

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.605
improvement of the system
with the government,

00:04:37.606 --> 00:04:39.495
like trying to be a linkage,

00:04:39.496 --> 00:04:41.230
that's another program we have.

00:04:41.231 --> 00:04:44.390
Child Friendly Cities, I
overheard some of you talking

00:04:44.391 --> 00:04:49.020
about what is that,
the smart cities.

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.760
In Child Friendly Cities,

00:04:50.761 --> 00:04:52.910
we are developing
a model of child

00:04:52.911 --> 00:04:56.090
friendly cities in 10 cities.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.270
This year we have
started with four cities

00:04:59.271 --> 00:05:01.750
in which we bring
in one platform,

00:05:01.751 --> 00:05:04.690
NGOs, government
officials of the city,

00:05:04.691 --> 00:05:07.575
the people of the place,

00:05:07.576 --> 00:05:08.900
children as well as on

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.270
the platform trying to
understand the problem of

00:05:11.271 --> 00:05:13.580
the children in the city so that

00:05:13.581 --> 00:05:16.385
they're able to take care of
the children in the city,

00:05:16.386 --> 00:05:18.535
making it much more
child-friendly,

00:05:18.536 --> 00:05:21.170
and we are telling
the smart city builders,

00:05:21.171 --> 00:05:23.270
if you don't include the element

00:05:23.271 --> 00:05:26.020
of child-friendliness
in the city,

00:05:26.021 --> 00:05:27.995
your city is not smart.

00:05:27.996 --> 00:05:30.590
IUA is also in
collaboration with us.

00:05:30.591 --> 00:05:31.880
We're trying to create

00:05:31.881 --> 00:05:34.040
a child-friendly environment
in the city so that

00:05:34.041 --> 00:05:35.870
children feel comfortable and

00:05:35.871 --> 00:05:37.560
safe, that's another program.

00:05:37.561 --> 00:05:40.495
Homelink Network is what I'm
going to be talking about.

00:05:40.496 --> 00:05:43.730
Standards of care is
another aspect of caring of

00:05:43.731 --> 00:05:48.325
children in the centers
where the children exists,

00:05:48.326 --> 00:05:50.120
where the children stay with

00:05:50.121 --> 00:05:51.980
us so that we are able to give

00:05:51.981 --> 00:05:56.125
them wonderful care for
them, building up standards.

00:05:56.126 --> 00:05:58.130
These are all in short,
some of the work that

00:05:58.131 --> 00:06:00.785
we do across India.

00:06:00.786 --> 00:06:03.560
Looking for collaboration
with the AI community.

00:06:03.561 --> 00:06:05.240
What are the three problems

00:06:05.241 --> 00:06:06.900
that I want to present to you?

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:10.110
The one is Run Away Children,

00:06:10.111 --> 00:06:12.865
another one is the Lost Children,

00:06:12.866 --> 00:06:14.615
another one is the Child Care.

00:06:14.616 --> 00:06:17.000
What is the problem?

00:06:17.001 --> 00:06:20.175
Every day, the statistic says,

00:06:20.176 --> 00:06:24.330
there are about 174 children
go missing in India.

00:06:24.331 --> 00:06:26.375
This is a world statistics.

00:06:26.376 --> 00:06:29.020
You know that the number
keeps increasing.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:32.689
Of late, you must have
heard about Bihar,

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:35.690
the nightmares the children

00:06:35.691 --> 00:06:38.680
went through in some of
the NGOs, they have been raped,

00:06:38.681 --> 00:06:40.380
even in the name
of- you went to say

00:06:40.381 --> 00:06:42.795
that you're running
an NGO for children is

00:06:42.796 --> 00:06:44.765
frightening these days because of

00:06:44.766 --> 00:06:46.880
even the traffickers get into

00:06:46.881 --> 00:06:49.435
the shoes of these NGO
and spoil the name.

00:06:49.436 --> 00:06:52.910
So, traffickers can come in
different ways and that is

00:06:52.911 --> 00:06:54.590
the danger for all these run away

00:06:54.591 --> 00:06:58.080
children as well as
for the lost children.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:04.105
The statistics again
says 1,011,569

00:07:04.106 --> 00:07:10.295
they were lost and about
55,625 remain unidentified.

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:11.975
This is the government data,

00:07:11.976 --> 00:07:14.080
we are not very sure
about that data.

00:07:14.081 --> 00:07:16.730
It is much more. So, this

00:07:16.731 --> 00:07:20.120
is the problem that I'm going
to be talking to you today.

00:07:20.121 --> 00:07:22.110
What is this lost child?

00:07:22.111 --> 00:07:27.950
Let's take the stages in which
a lost child goes through.

00:07:27.951 --> 00:07:32.090
When the lost child
comes into the street or

00:07:32.091 --> 00:07:33.830
the railway station or

00:07:33.831 --> 00:07:36.770
the child is actually going
with the parents somewhere,

00:07:36.771 --> 00:07:40.390
and then the child
gets lost, it happens,

00:07:40.391 --> 00:07:43.910
it loses track of the parent
or the child comes

00:07:43.911 --> 00:07:46.820
with some of friends
who want to see

00:07:46.821 --> 00:07:49.875
the city or within
the city they get lost.

00:07:49.876 --> 00:07:53.720
And they are just loitering
around in the platforms of

00:07:53.721 --> 00:07:55.730
the railway stations or

00:07:55.731 --> 00:07:57.980
in the bus stand or
in the marketplaces.

00:07:57.981 --> 00:07:59.335
Our staff are there,

00:07:59.336 --> 00:08:00.830
we have booths even in

00:08:00.831 --> 00:08:03.570
Bangalore bus station
as well as Bosco,

00:08:03.571 --> 00:08:05.860
here in Bangalore it's called

00:08:05.861 --> 00:08:08.570
Bosco under the title
Bosco, it is functioning.

00:08:08.571 --> 00:08:10.040
They have booths there in

00:08:10.041 --> 00:08:12.455
the railway station platforms
as well as and our staff

00:08:12.456 --> 00:08:13.985
are there 24 hours

00:08:13.986 --> 00:08:16.190
trying to monitor if
any of these children.

00:08:16.191 --> 00:08:18.500
They also educate
the caring community.

00:08:18.501 --> 00:08:20.510
The platform sweepers and

00:08:20.511 --> 00:08:22.640
other people are also educated to

00:08:22.641 --> 00:08:24.425
identify these kinds of children

00:08:24.426 --> 00:08:27.320
and bring the children
to these booths.

00:08:27.321 --> 00:08:31.370
To the extent I heard
a story from a lady who

00:08:31.371 --> 00:08:35.835
was involved in the flesh trade,
doing prostitution.

00:08:35.836 --> 00:08:39.530
She identifies
sometimes girls whom

00:08:39.531 --> 00:08:41.490
her superior would take and

00:08:41.491 --> 00:08:43.715
then put her into prostitution,

00:08:43.716 --> 00:08:47.370
she would rescue and tell
the child don't be here,

00:08:47.371 --> 00:08:49.350
It's very dangerous, don't

00:08:49.351 --> 00:08:51.555
live the life which I am living,

00:08:51.556 --> 00:08:54.355
better go to that booth,
they will help you out.

00:08:54.356 --> 00:08:57.160
So, that's how the society
is interested in.

00:08:57.161 --> 00:08:58.385
Picking up these kinds of

00:08:58.386 --> 00:09:00.530
children and bringing
them to safety.

00:09:00.531 --> 00:09:03.040
Trafficker also, they
are also present on

00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:05.740
the street trying to pick
up these kind of children.

00:09:05.741 --> 00:09:09.950
So, when the child comes into
the NGO or the caretaker,

00:09:09.951 --> 00:09:12.225
is identified by
the NGO or the public,

00:09:12.226 --> 00:09:13.520
they're making effort in

00:09:13.521 --> 00:09:15.380
searching for the child
and their parents.

00:09:15.381 --> 00:09:18.925
When the child who is
lost comes to you,

00:09:18.926 --> 00:09:22.160
most of the time
the child will tell you,

00:09:22.161 --> 00:09:27.400
you know uncle, I am
from that temple.

00:09:27.401 --> 00:09:29.520
You know there is a temple,

00:09:29.521 --> 00:09:32.750
near that temple is my house.

00:09:32.751 --> 00:09:37.250
Auntie, we are coming

00:09:37.251 --> 00:09:40.310
from school and
that name of the school.

00:09:40.311 --> 00:09:43.420
Hardly few words,
a few sentences,

00:09:43.421 --> 00:09:46.385
which is what the child
will remember and then

00:09:46.386 --> 00:09:49.730
the NGO worker has
to start tracking.

00:09:49.731 --> 00:09:51.420
Who are these NGO workers?

00:09:51.421 --> 00:09:53.319
They're just simple graduates

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:56.490
maximum or 10th
passer plus two pass.

00:09:56.491 --> 00:09:58.865
This is what the NGO can afford.

00:09:58.866 --> 00:10:03.780
So, these people that are able

00:10:03.781 --> 00:10:05.900
to track these children and

00:10:05.901 --> 00:10:08.715
then with these little
information that they give,

00:10:08.716 --> 00:10:10.830
they go to the website,
they Google,

00:10:10.831 --> 00:10:12.485
they search for the
police station,

00:10:12.486 --> 00:10:13.885
they look for
the complain and they

00:10:13.886 --> 00:10:15.805
try to send them back.

00:10:15.806 --> 00:10:18.620
In the meantime,
the parents are going to

00:10:18.621 --> 00:10:21.500
the nearby police station
and then they're going and

00:10:21.501 --> 00:10:23.955
lodging a complain and

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:27.310
they are trying to
search for the child.

00:10:27.311 --> 00:10:31.785
Maximum, the police will
receive the file in FIR,

00:10:31.786 --> 00:10:33.210
mostly they don't do.

00:10:33.211 --> 00:10:34.520
Our own the record says

00:10:34.521 --> 00:10:36.830
about 60 to 70 percent
of the people

00:10:36.831 --> 00:10:39.555
who lose their children
don't file an FIR,

00:10:39.556 --> 00:10:41.835
first information
report with the police

00:10:41.836 --> 00:10:45.000
because they are
afraid of the police,

00:10:45.001 --> 00:10:46.525
if they're ordinary people.

00:10:46.526 --> 00:10:49.030
If they are rich people, police
will go around the line,

00:10:49.031 --> 00:10:51.575
search for the child.
Otherwise, nothing happens.

00:10:51.576 --> 00:10:55.610
The FIR sleeps in the database
of the police and

00:10:55.611 --> 00:10:58.660
the NGOs whatever the information

00:10:58.661 --> 00:11:01.210
about the child which
they're collecting,

00:11:01.211 --> 00:11:03.830
it is sleeping in
the database of the child.

00:11:03.831 --> 00:11:07.420
Yes. They also know
which is the child who

00:11:07.421 --> 00:11:11.230
is lost and they know
who is the child,

00:11:11.231 --> 00:11:12.940
how they can know the child.

00:11:12.941 --> 00:11:14.225
They have their own strategies,

00:11:14.226 --> 00:11:16.190
as the NGOs have
their strategies.

00:11:16.191 --> 00:11:19.840
The child is lost and
so it falls prey to

00:11:19.841 --> 00:11:22.040
these kind of trap that they

00:11:22.041 --> 00:11:24.630
set and so gets into the problem,

00:11:24.631 --> 00:11:29.440
that's why the time the child
lands on the street

00:11:29.441 --> 00:11:33.460
until it is rescued is
that very crucial time

00:11:33.461 --> 00:11:36.275
you need to spend in order
to rescue the child.

00:11:36.276 --> 00:11:39.090
Have I answered your question?

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:46.230
This strategy is- it

00:11:46.231 --> 00:11:49.890
is- winning over the child
is their strategy.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.005
By giving a sweet,

00:11:53.006 --> 00:11:56.640
by promising work, by promising
to take them back home,

00:11:56.641 --> 00:11:57.875
if the child is crying,

00:11:57.876 --> 00:12:00.280
whatever the child is addressing

00:12:00.281 --> 00:12:04.220
is the answer that they
will give accordingly.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.940
Yeah. So, there is
a information about

00:12:08.941 --> 00:12:12.895
the child is lying in
the database of the NGO,

00:12:12.896 --> 00:12:15.340
the inflammation of the
complaint is lying in

00:12:15.341 --> 00:12:19.015
the database of the
CWC or the police,

00:12:19.016 --> 00:12:23.030
CWC does not have its own
database which is functional.

00:12:23.031 --> 00:12:24.730
And the parents are searching,

00:12:24.731 --> 00:12:26.515
and other NGOs might,

00:12:26.516 --> 00:12:27.680
they might even go into

00:12:27.681 --> 00:12:30.695
some other NGOs and give
some complaints and it is

00:12:30.696 --> 00:12:33.395
the database also
is there lying all

00:12:33.396 --> 00:12:36.645
separated not united in any way.

00:12:36.646 --> 00:12:39.070
The challenges for
this lost child is how we

00:12:39.071 --> 00:12:41.715
can reduce the time in
restoring the child.

00:12:41.716 --> 00:12:44.900
The child tells you few words
with that how we can

00:12:44.901 --> 00:12:48.060
search the police
station or the database,

00:12:48.061 --> 00:12:50.210
how we can connect
that's a big challenge.

00:12:50.211 --> 00:12:53.205
How can we help in tracing
the parents or guardian

00:12:53.206 --> 00:12:56.675
with the words
uttered by the child?

00:12:56.676 --> 00:12:58.364
It will just tell you school,

00:12:58.365 --> 00:12:59.880
the child will tell you school,

00:12:59.881 --> 00:13:01.430
or temple, or sweet shop,

00:13:01.431 --> 00:13:04.000
or bus stand, friend's name,
father's name,

00:13:04.001 --> 00:13:07.270
mother's name, these are
all minimum you could get.

00:13:07.271 --> 00:13:10.355
How we can connect
various databases,

00:13:10.356 --> 00:13:12.695
this is a big challenge
that we have.

00:13:12.696 --> 00:13:14.520
How can we make
the distributed data

00:13:14.521 --> 00:13:17.020
of child available
to police and CWC,

00:13:17.021 --> 00:13:19.890
the child welfare committee
in each district who

00:13:19.891 --> 00:13:22.950
can make a decision to
get the child back?

00:13:22.951 --> 00:13:25.200
The analysis report
for the NGOs take

00:13:25.201 --> 00:13:28.680
action which area
more children are coming and,

00:13:28.681 --> 00:13:32.370
how we can solve
the problem etc. Yes.

00:13:32.371 --> 00:13:37.570
&gt;&gt; [inaudible].

00:13:37.571 --> 00:13:40.515
&gt;&gt; It depends that's why he
said there is a lost child,

00:13:40.516 --> 00:13:42.365
there is a runaway child.

00:13:42.366 --> 00:13:44.860
The lost child wants go home,

00:13:44.861 --> 00:13:47.380
a runaway child does
not want to go home

00:13:47.381 --> 00:13:51.055
because of smaller problems
of fight at home possibly.

00:13:51.056 --> 00:13:54.295
So, the time factor

00:13:54.296 --> 00:13:56.905
in taking the child back
home is a big challenge.

00:13:56.906 --> 00:13:58.765
Last year in Chennai,
for example,

00:13:58.766 --> 00:14:01.830
we had a child from
Chhattisgarh, nine years ago,

00:14:01.831 --> 00:14:04.770
the child came to the NGO,
they made effort,

00:14:04.771 --> 00:14:06.535
they took the child
once or twice to

00:14:06.536 --> 00:14:10.005
Chhattisgarh ,they could not
identify the child's place.

00:14:10.006 --> 00:14:12.740
Okay? So, they put him back here,

00:14:12.741 --> 00:14:14.855
educated in Tamil medium,

00:14:14.856 --> 00:14:16.765
the child reached
up to ninth class,

00:14:16.766 --> 00:14:19.465
the child every year would
reveal some information.

00:14:19.466 --> 00:14:22.380
With that they made effort
when he was in ninth class,

00:14:22.381 --> 00:14:23.810
they traced the parent.

00:14:23.811 --> 00:14:26.850
Yeah. After nine years
or eight years,

00:14:26.851 --> 00:14:28.110
it's a joyful event,

00:14:28.111 --> 00:14:29.990
but the child has
already studied in

00:14:29.991 --> 00:14:33.470
Tamil medium and he cannot
go back to Chhattisgarh.

00:14:33.471 --> 00:14:35.300
So, this is a challenge.

00:14:35.301 --> 00:14:37.040
What is the mistake of the NGO?

00:14:37.041 --> 00:14:42.870
They couldn't help it out
and the parent has tried,

00:14:42.871 --> 00:14:45.050
but the databases,
the information is not

00:14:45.051 --> 00:14:47.765
connected and so we are not
able to settle back home.

00:14:47.766 --> 00:14:52.555
Such stories do come up
every year in every city.

00:14:52.556 --> 00:14:56.330
The type of number of children
who come in, for example,

00:14:56.331 --> 00:14:59.995
it's easy how much
a NGO can employ,

00:14:59.996 --> 00:15:03.180
you'll get 40 children in
Bangladesh, for example,

00:15:03.181 --> 00:15:06.450
40 to 60 new children
come every day into

00:15:06.451 --> 00:15:10.580
the city and counseling
40 to 60 children,

00:15:10.581 --> 00:15:13.365
what is a challenge and
an amount of time that is spent.

00:15:13.366 --> 00:15:15.605
These are all challenges
that we need to.

00:15:15.606 --> 00:15:17.395
Restoring a runaway child.

00:15:17.396 --> 00:15:18.805
Runaway child will come and

00:15:18.806 --> 00:15:21.115
change everything
of his identity.

00:15:21.116 --> 00:15:23.340
The child comes to the street,

00:15:23.341 --> 00:15:25.300
it is lucky that you're able to

00:15:25.301 --> 00:15:27.435
identify and bring
the child home,

00:15:27.436 --> 00:15:30.365
and then when you
start counseling,

00:15:30.366 --> 00:15:32.880
if he is from a Muslim community,

00:15:32.881 --> 00:15:34.860
he will say, "I am James."

00:15:34.861 --> 00:15:37.755
He'll change his name,
he'll change his religion.

00:15:37.756 --> 00:15:39.840
"What is your name?" "I am Ram."

00:15:39.841 --> 00:15:41.710
But he must be Mohammed actually.

00:15:41.711 --> 00:15:44.670
After 16 years, we found out that

00:15:44.671 --> 00:15:48.545
one child was
a Muslim not a Hindu.

00:15:48.546 --> 00:15:50.455
This is how they will change.

00:15:50.456 --> 00:15:51.530
They'll change their identity,

00:15:51.531 --> 00:15:53.440
they'll forget
their identity also.

00:15:53.441 --> 00:15:55.190
So, this is a challenge there.

00:15:55.191 --> 00:15:57.885
In this place of runaway child,

00:15:57.886 --> 00:15:59.410
collecting a biometrics and

00:15:59.411 --> 00:16:01.770
identifying possibly
is a solution.

00:16:01.771 --> 00:16:02.590
That's where we are running

00:16:02.591 --> 00:16:05.630
an experiment with
this biometric.

00:16:05.631 --> 00:16:09.550
This disputed database,
Aadhar is having its data,

00:16:09.551 --> 00:16:12.360
but how we can connect
it, very difficult.

00:16:12.361 --> 00:16:14.530
Then Homelink has its own data,

00:16:14.531 --> 00:16:16.260
TrackChild has it's own data,

00:16:16.261 --> 00:16:18.110
Khoya Paya has its own data.

00:16:18.111 --> 00:16:21.650
All these are having
independent data not connected,

00:16:21.651 --> 00:16:23.535
but they are willing to join

00:16:23.536 --> 00:16:25.930
hands in order to
solve the problem.

00:16:25.931 --> 00:16:28.035
The challenge is this again,

00:16:28.036 --> 00:16:30.310
which bio-metric will
work for the children?

00:16:30.311 --> 00:16:32.310
Others says it will not work,

00:16:32.311 --> 00:16:33.920
so what is the solution?

00:16:33.921 --> 00:16:36.360
Can we not create
a common platform in

00:16:36.361 --> 00:16:38.890
which all these biometrics
can be tested out?

00:16:38.891 --> 00:16:40.220
This is what we had been

00:16:40.221 --> 00:16:42.110
discussing for
the past two years with

00:16:42.111 --> 00:16:46.365
Microsoft and some solution
or some model has emerged,

00:16:46.366 --> 00:16:47.985
we have not yet implemented.

00:16:47.986 --> 00:16:49.560
Can the AI platform provide

00:16:49.561 --> 00:16:51.360
enough data for the counselor to

00:16:51.361 --> 00:16:52.900
identify the child and

00:16:52.901 --> 00:16:55.170
help the child to
get back home soon?

00:16:55.171 --> 00:16:58.005
Because the pattern in
which the children talk,

00:16:58.006 --> 00:16:59.950
sometimes it is the same.

00:16:59.951 --> 00:17:02.220
So, can these AI give

00:17:02.221 --> 00:17:05.660
the counselor who is an ordinary
person with their degree?

00:17:05.661 --> 00:17:09.095
Should be assisted
in order to identify

00:17:09.096 --> 00:17:10.275
what category and what are

00:17:10.276 --> 00:17:12.495
the problems
this child is saying,

00:17:12.496 --> 00:17:15.620
and what possibly in
the experiences that

00:17:15.621 --> 00:17:18.855
we have with the data
whatever is the solution.

00:17:18.856 --> 00:17:20.750
Can AI provide data to assess

00:17:20.751 --> 00:17:23.240
the problem of the child
based on his behavior,

00:17:23.241 --> 00:17:25.085
reaction, words used, and

00:17:25.086 --> 00:17:28.045
accordingly to the counseling
and correction process?

00:17:28.046 --> 00:17:30.630
Is a challenge. Under care

00:17:30.631 --> 00:17:32.760
and protection
the third problem. Yes.

00:17:32.761 --> 00:17:33.890
&gt;&gt; [inaudible].

00:17:33.891 --> 00:17:35.395
&gt;&gt; One minute, I'll finish.

00:17:35.396 --> 00:17:37.240
The care and protection is,

00:17:37.241 --> 00:17:40.675
again, the child is
staying with us,

00:17:40.676 --> 00:17:43.175
he maybe an orphan
and he has nobody,

00:17:43.176 --> 00:17:44.980
we know that he has
nobody and so we

00:17:44.981 --> 00:17:47.100
start taking care of the child.

00:17:47.101 --> 00:17:49.645
But whatever may
be the situation,

00:17:49.646 --> 00:17:51.640
in a particular place
like Bangalore,

00:17:51.641 --> 00:17:53.545
they may be very
innovative in taking

00:17:53.546 --> 00:17:55.590
care of the child on physical,

00:17:55.591 --> 00:17:57.945
development, social,
emotional, intellectual,

00:17:57.946 --> 00:17:59.500
spiritual, care et cetera.

00:17:59.501 --> 00:18:02.170
All these level, each one
will be innovative.

00:18:02.171 --> 00:18:05.550
But all these innovation
will lie within one NGO.

00:18:05.551 --> 00:18:07.415
Suppose these all get

00:18:07.416 --> 00:18:10.485
formulated into
an analysis and we are

00:18:10.486 --> 00:18:12.950
able to identify
these innovation and put

00:18:12.951 --> 00:18:15.660
it as a standard for
the whole of India,

00:18:15.661 --> 00:18:17.105
or the whole of the world,

00:18:17.106 --> 00:18:19.740
and then measure accordingly
whenever you ask

00:18:19.741 --> 00:18:21.180
a few inputs that NGO

00:18:21.181 --> 00:18:23.720
people are ready to get
and free data it inside,

00:18:23.721 --> 00:18:25.390
and with that every quarter

00:18:25.391 --> 00:18:27.045
we are able to assess and say,

00:18:27.046 --> 00:18:29.570
this child is not
okay emotionally,

00:18:29.571 --> 00:18:32.190
this child is not located
in the knowledge wise,

00:18:32.191 --> 00:18:33.610
and then take measures.

00:18:33.611 --> 00:18:36.180
So, when we are able
to give them feedback,

00:18:36.181 --> 00:18:37.355
they will always act.

00:18:37.356 --> 00:18:38.870
There is every chance

00:18:38.871 --> 00:18:40.545
that there is
a corrective measures.

00:18:40.546 --> 00:18:41.925
So, with the data available,

00:18:41.926 --> 00:18:43.325
can we not provide this?

00:18:43.326 --> 00:18:44.130
This is a challenge.

00:18:44.131 --> 00:18:46.220
Can we check with
few input variables

00:18:46.221 --> 00:18:49.335
whether the child is progressing
in all forms of growth?

00:18:49.336 --> 00:18:51.055
Can we create standards?

00:18:51.056 --> 00:18:53.785
What are the new challenges
that are emerging with that?

00:18:53.786 --> 00:18:56.885
Because every year the type
of children who come

00:18:56.886 --> 00:19:00.780
and the type of challenges
that they throw is new,

00:19:00.781 --> 00:19:05.235
and the corrective measures
cannot be same.

00:19:05.236 --> 00:19:06.565
So, we have with us

00:19:06.566 --> 00:19:09.430
about three lacks
data in our database.

00:19:09.431 --> 00:19:13.335
In the past six to 10 years
we have been working

00:19:13.336 --> 00:19:17.265
with the visual basic starting
with the debasing visual.

00:19:17.266 --> 00:19:21.805
Basically, I've been having
databases and now we have

00:19:21.806 --> 00:19:23.790
in Microsoft Azure platform

00:19:23.791 --> 00:19:26.775
also data about
three lakhs we have,

00:19:26.776 --> 00:19:29.825
and we have home placed
about one lakh odd,

00:19:29.826 --> 00:19:32.850
and institutionalized
about 67,000.

00:19:32.851 --> 00:19:34.845
They're in contact about 13,000,

00:19:34.846 --> 00:19:36.370
all these has only entered data

00:19:36.371 --> 00:19:39.735
not all the NGOs enter their
data,this is entered data.

00:19:39.736 --> 00:19:42.820
But the actual work is
enormous and the children who

00:19:42.821 --> 00:19:46.950
died also these data also
we are able to maintain.

00:19:46.951 --> 00:19:49.220
The missing complaints we have

00:19:49.221 --> 00:19:51.010
received in our institutes across

00:19:51.011 --> 00:19:55.860
India we have about 8,338 traced,

00:19:55.861 --> 00:19:58.720
complaint received
is about 19,300.

00:19:58.721 --> 00:20:03.790
So, with our own manual systems
of search et cetera,

00:20:03.791 --> 00:20:06.250
we are able to
solve this problem.

00:20:06.251 --> 00:20:07.955
This is the design that has

00:20:07.956 --> 00:20:09.850
been proposed by
Microsoft that we

00:20:09.851 --> 00:20:16.160
been working with in us
with one of the guy.

00:20:16.161 --> 00:20:17.980
So, he was suggesting to us,

00:20:17.981 --> 00:20:19.540
if you go with this design,

00:20:19.541 --> 00:20:21.110
you'll be able to
connect the database,

00:20:21.111 --> 00:20:22.470
we're still dreaming about it

00:20:22.471 --> 00:20:26.560
hope it happens soon. Thank you.

00:20:26.561 --> 00:20:29.345
&gt;&gt; Thank you [inaudible]
for the inspiring story.

00:20:29.346 --> 00:20:31.150
Now in the interest
of time and making

00:20:31.151 --> 00:20:32.755
sure that everybody
gets a fair chance,

00:20:32.756 --> 00:20:34.175
we'll take one question.

00:20:34.176 --> 00:20:38.235
So, I can see, yeah. One please.

00:20:38.236 --> 00:20:41.365
&gt;&gt; Thank you very much.
I have a question.

00:20:41.366 --> 00:20:44.950
What has been your experience
with the police

00:20:44.951 --> 00:20:49.180
and have you been able
to access their data?

00:20:49.181 --> 00:20:51.695
How useful has it been?

00:20:51.696 --> 00:20:54.915
&gt;&gt; Our experience
with police has been

00:20:54.916 --> 00:20:58.795
buried because some states
they're quite open,

00:20:58.796 --> 00:21:00.355
some states they say we have

00:21:00.356 --> 00:21:01.925
our own database because

00:21:01.926 --> 00:21:03.630
each one is married
to their own data,

00:21:03.631 --> 00:21:04.680
that is why we came up with

00:21:04.681 --> 00:21:11.285
a shared model and each database
has its own specifics.

00:21:11.286 --> 00:21:14.180
See for example BBA [inaudible] ,

00:21:14.181 --> 00:21:19.285
they have specific data
on on child labor.

00:21:19.286 --> 00:21:22.020
We don't need all that
for identifying children,

00:21:22.021 --> 00:21:23.740
we need only few elements.

00:21:23.741 --> 00:21:26.510
Police have lots of
other information

00:21:26.511 --> 00:21:29.075
which is not required for
identifying the child,

00:21:29.076 --> 00:21:31.555
so, we are only dialoguing
with them and saying,

00:21:31.556 --> 00:21:33.400
you don't need to
share everything,

00:21:33.401 --> 00:21:34.660
you don't need to share

00:21:34.661 --> 00:21:37.750
common elements which will be
helpful for identification,

00:21:37.751 --> 00:21:39.960
we think that with this process,

00:21:39.961 --> 00:21:41.140
it will be possible.

00:21:41.141 --> 00:21:44.710
Some police, some states
they have been very very

00:21:44.711 --> 00:21:48.595
helpful in implementing
together, yes.

00:21:48.596 --> 00:21:51.020
Bangalore for example,
we share data.

00:21:51.021 --> 00:21:52.215
At least in Excel form

00:21:52.216 --> 00:21:54.500
they keep sharing
among each other,

00:21:54.501 --> 00:21:56.135
the two databases [inaudible] .

00:21:56.136 --> 00:22:03.440
&gt;&gt; Thank you [inaudible].

